In article <379D5F42.2781@dnr.qld.gov.au>, Keith Moodie <moodiek@dnr.qld.gov.au> writes:

>We have added a second SCSI controller to a Digital Personal Workstation
>433au running 4.0D

While you don't have to rebuild the kernel to add disks or tapes
to an existing SCSI adapter, you do have to rebuild the kernel
for a new SCSI adapter.  You can try to edit the configuration
file by hand if you know the PCI bus and slot the new adapter is
in or you can just boot genvmunix and let doconfig write a new
configuration file for you.

While the generic kernel is booting, you'll want to watch the
boot messages to make sure the new adapter hasn't changed the
device numbering of the existing devices.  Once the kernel knows
to look for the new adapter, it will find whatever tapes and
disks are on it and in V4 will create the appropriate special
files.

>There is one RAID controller on this bus at SCSI Id 1
>
>
>My problem is how do I find out what /dev/rz... to MAKEDEV

The RAID behaves reasonably, the devices should be created for
you when the system boots.
