>and hopefully a quick answer :~)
>How can I backup the complete system in DECUnix4.0d. I've been trying to use
>vdump but only seem to be able to backup individual file sets.
>

In principle you can tar from / and recurse, or perhaps cpio.  tar and
cpio may not be the save format you want to use.  Most tools which ship
with UNIX which back up one partition.  There may be COTS products which
will do what you want.

But why backup the complete system as one?  If you loose a disk you'll
want a conveneint way to restore only the partitions on that disk.

