During start up, you should see some numbers across the top of the screen.
at this point start pressing ^C. Keep pressing this (release and re-press it)
and eventually the machine will stop at the >>> prompt.
From there you can avoid this problem by changing the environment variable
auto_action. Type

set auto_action halt

to cause the machine to wait at the >>> prompt each power on.
If after many tries you fail to get the ^C trick to work, then
disconnect the power to the boot disk and switch on, the machine will
fail to boot and leave you at the >>> prompt.

Then change auto_action and reconnect the drive.

Sorry if I misunderstood your previous post,
Adam

PS to return to the auto-boot mode that you have now, you will
