> The above devices are showing as rz0, rz16, rz17, rzb17, rz18, rz19
> respectivly
> 
> --
> 
> Keith Moodie,
> EMail: moodiek@dnr.qld.gov.au

The magic calculation is bus*8+target, eg.

bus = 0, target = 0 ==>rz0
bus = 2, target = 1 ==>rz17

Target = SCSI ID in case you were confused.

So, I'd expect devices on bus 1 to be rz8-rz15, depending on the SCSI
IDs in use. 
Regards,
John Hill



