Sorry to follow up my own post.

Of course the bits I forgot until I got your e-mail and can now add are...
1 scu shows no sign of the new scsi card
2 scu shows no sign of the new disk
3 bus 1 is the second IDE but in a personal Workstation


So, do a kernel rebuild to get the card added to the kernel
    shut down to srm (type init 0)
    boot from generic kernel (type boot -file genvmunix )
    rebuild kernel  (type doconfig ; follow the prompts)
    copy the current kernel to /vmunix.old
    copy the new kernel (/sys/HOSTNAME/vmunix) to /
    shut down to srm (type init 0)
    boot normally (type boot)

When this is done your scu scan edt, scu show edt will show the disk
it should be on bus 3 and so be 3*8 +1 = rz25

Sorry I didn't spot this first time,
Hope this helps
Adam

