Kim, Hyunchul (kimhc@inzen.com) wrote:

: I'm writing a program which examines the system calls of other processes.

: With "/proc" file system and some ioctl calls(),
: I succeeded for it to make another process stop when system call.
: But I don't know how to get the parameters of the system call and
: return value or error flag of it.

Syscall number is in the register 0 (of gregset_t.regs obtained by 
PIOCSREG). Syscall parameters are in the registers 16 to 19 (decimal).
Return code OR error code is in the register 0 (and, I guess, also 1
if you are doing pipe() - but I had not checked this). The meaning of
the return code is given by the value of the register 19: zero means
successful completion (with the return code in reg. 0); non-zero is
error condition, with errno value in reg. 0.

Regards,

/Serge.P

--
