This depends on how the files were deleted...

If one were to delete files using the CDE File Manager (or something of
the like), then they MIGHT be able to recover those files from the
Wastebasket. As long as they didn't "empty" their Wastebasket.

If one were to delete their files using good old rm, then the recovery
of those files would be highly dependent on whether or not a good backup
is available. If these "very important files" were system related (rm -R
/usr), then I hope there is either a good backup or the original
installation CD's handy. 

