Another possibility is see if you can find some file system tools. If
the system/disk is not accessed much, and you do not have a high level
of security on it, then the files might be "recovered" using the
appropriate hacks. I'm afraid I do not know of any hacks right off...

If the system is heavily used, or is in a "high security" mode, then the
files are probably overwritten or were erased at the moment of deletion.
Which brings us back to having a good backup...

It does not take much to set up a cron job to have files tarred/dumped
to disk or tape once a day.
