>which versions, and why?

I've never had the problem myself, so I don't know which versions
may have a problem.  As to why...  Normal day to day activity
doesn't exercise every nook and cranny of a file system.  Subtle
corruptions from old bugs (or current ones) can creep into a file
system.  The data migration that occurs with a rmvol should
exercise every bit of the domain on the device being removed.
If such a corruption exists on that device, it may cause the
rest of the domain, and thus you, grief.

