In <37973757.C2C6FA27@compaq.com>
Craig Neth <craig.neth@compaq.com> writes:

>The Tru64 runtime loader has a list of 'known'
>places to look for libraries

Indeed it does. :-)


>We'll consider it if fills a need...  Help me understand the need.

Well, from where I'm sitting the problem is that that list of known
places can't be expanded by adding local directories.

For example, on our systems we have a directory called /local/libpaths
which contains symlinks to all the shared libraries we've installed for
locally compiled software.  It would be *really* handy to be able to
tell the runtime loader to look there, as can easily be done on Linux.

Instead, we have to modify the makefiles for each package to do the
equivalent of

   cc -o foo foo.c -L/local/libpaths -lbar -Wl,-rpath,/local/libpaths
 
Clearly this works, but just adding /local/libpaths to the runtime
loader's search path would be ever so much more convenient. :-)

