Wan-Teh Chang (wtc@netscape.com) wrote:
: I read in comp.programming.threads that
: on Tru64 UNIX one can mmap /dev/sysdev0
: to read the system clock without a system call.
: I can't find any info about this technique in the
: man pages.

Upon examining /dev/MAKEDEV and /sys/include/kern/sysdev_info.h,
it appears that you should:

a) as root, do: 'cd /dev/;./MAKEDEV sysdev0; chmod go+r sysdev0'
b) do p = mmap(0,sizeof(struct sysdef_info),PROT_READ,0,
               open("/dev/sysdev0",O_RDONLY),0)
c) get your time at ((struct sysdef_info*)p)->tv)

Do not forget to add appropriate error checking.

Caveat: I had not tested this.

/Serge.P

