Digital/Tru64 UNIX only runs on hefty enough Alpha based systems (SRM
console). Now, if you have a hefty enough Alpha lying around, you can
use it to run NT, OpenVMS, Digital UNIX, Linux Alpha, and NetBSD. To top
it off, it's already a 64-bit machine, whereas Intel's 64-bit machine is
still vaporware.

