Very similar setup here: 100BaseTx (full-duplex) network running on 3COM SSII 3300,
500au's using AdvFS. Here are some timings (using a *single* 7200RPM 4.3Gb drive on 
the remote side):

TCP mem-mem:            11.24Mbyte/second
NFSv3 sequential read:   3.39Mbyte/second
NFSv3 sequential write:  4.14Mbyte/second

The NFSv3 write speed is in fact within 25% of the local disk write speed
(unfortunately, I do not have the exact number at hand). Also note that
writing is faster than reading.

: The problem is a performance problem. Reading from the NFS server is quite
: fast, but writing, especially with many smaller files, very slow.  Untarring
: a typical source code tarball is about factor 10 more slow if the tarball is
: stroed locally and being untarred to a directory on the saver than if the
: tarball is on the server and being untarred to a local disk. 

Check your cabling, network settings, and network configuration. Full-duplex
vs. half-duplex mismatch is one common source of problems with NFS performance;
having more than two NICs on a single full-duplex segment in another. Start
with:

netstat -i ; netstat -s ; netstat -s -I tu0

