As far as I understand it, AdvFS is nosync by default (it uses journalling
to take care of filesystem integrity). There is a lot of parameters which
can affect AdvFS performance (just look up the AdvFS section in the system
tuning manual ;-). sys_check may be able to suggest some in your case. We
have:

advfs:
   AdvfsMaxDevQLen=16

in our /etc/sysconfigtab, which really helps. There are also parameters
controlling write consolidation and amount of dirty data AdvFS buffers
can hold before syncing them to disk ...

I seem to remember from your previous post that you have multiple spindles
in your NFS-exported partition, right? Do you use LSM or just put several
physical into a single AdvFS domain?

