Ryurick M. Hristev wrote:

> Hello all,
>
> Please excuse a very dumb question :-) but could somebody tell me
> how do I change the root home directory so something more sane than / ?
> (there are several reasons for why I don't like it)

        I created /root, then copied every file and directory (cp -r for
files; cp -rp for required account directories) that looked like a
necessity for superuser into /root (I guessed which ones and haven't
noticed any shell or permission problems).  I then edited /etc/passwd to
show /root for the superuser account, using the CDE text editor.

        One problem:  I had already initiated Netscape in the old
location, and Netscape would not recognize or use the copied
/root/.netscape directory in the new location.  The solution was to create
the link .netscape----->/root/.netscape in /.  Netscape now executes
normally in the new root account.

Steve Stoddard




