Patrick Michel wrote in message <377AA4A5.115D5002@gcs.ch>...
>Can anyone tell me how to add a second and a third ethernet
network card
>
>to my DecUnix 4.0d Server after the OS is already installed?
>
>ifconfig shows me only the first Card (tu0).
>
>Also the Network Configuration Manager shows me only the first
one.
>
>thanks for help
>
If you can see the devices at the console level (>>> show
config ) then all you need is a kernel rebuild (boot from
genvmunix, doconfig, cp /sys/$HOSTNAME/vmunix / , reboot).. if
not then you need to tell us what type of network cards and what
type of Alpha...

Hope this helps
Adam

PS. if they are ISA or EISA cards then you need to use special
utilities to configure the cards before unix boots. (ECU, iconfig
isacfg...)





