Frederick:

  The problem is you are mmap'ing beyond the end of the file.
  The file you've opened is zero-length.  The mmap() call didn't
  return an error because there is some standard which requires Tru64
  to not issue an error when mmap'ing beyond the end of a file.

  The solution is to grow the file before you try accessing it.
  One easy way is to lseek to some desired offset and then write a byte.
  For example, add something like this to your program:


    long fill = -1;

    ret = lseek(fd,20,SEEK_SET);
    if (ret < 0) {
        perror("lseek error");
        exit(1);
    }

    ret = write(fd,&fill,4);
    if (ret < 0) {
        perror("write error");
        exit(1);
    }

Joe Mario




